id: pm-cflhoj
title: Reindex coverage test leaks semantic refresh HTTP beyond its mock lifetime
description: "The residual reindex branch test reproducibly exceeds the 30-second gate because it creates items after configuring remote semantic endpoints but before installing the shared semantic HTTP fixture. Background mutation refresh escapes the intended mock boundary and waits on network retries. Keep every semantic side effect deterministic and local, and reduce the focused test below the gate timeout without weakening assertions."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-04T18:54:48.188Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T19:54:40.891Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-04T19:54:40.424Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-04T19:54:40.424Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: The residual reindex test never reaches external semantic endpoints; focused reindex coverage completes below 30 seconds; full 100 percent coverage remains unchanged; the shared semantic mock owns every mutation-triggered semantic side effect.
goal: Deterministic offline test gates
objective: Keep semantic reindex coverage independent of host network and provider configuration
value: Coverage failures remain actionable instead of waiting on detached HTTP retries
impact: The focused residual case falls from repeated 49 to 98 second failures to about one second
outcome: Mutation refresh is explicitly cache-only inside the reindex-specific branch test while reindex HTTP behavior remains covered by its typed fixture
why_now: The mandatory full coverage gate reproduced the timeout twice during this delivery tranche
parent: pm-92if
resolution: "The residual reindex test sets mutation refresh to cache_only before fixture creation, leaving explicit reindex HTTP behavior under the intended mock."
expected_result: "No external semantic requests occur before the reindex HTTP fixture is active, and the focused case completes below 30 seconds."
actual_result: Focused linked execution passed in 705ms test time and 2.87s total; direct full coverage passed 100/100/100/100.
